 cite9†Name Search†lawyers.findlaw.com L29:   * cite10†Browse Legal Issues†lawyers.findlaw.com L30:   * cite11†Browse Law Firms†lawyers.findlaw.com L31:   * cite12†Support†lawyers.findlaw.com L32: \nL33: City, ZIP Code or County\nL34: [Input:  ]\nL35: \nL36: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL37: \nL38: Enter either your legal issue or location to continue\nL39: \nL40: Find a Lawyer\nL41: \nL42: Search by Legal Topic\nL43: \nL44: [Input]\nL45: \nL46: Enter legal topic\nL47: \nL48: Get the Information\nL49: # JACOBSON v. HEALTHCARE FINANCIAL SERVICES INC (2008)\nL50: \nL51: ## United States Court of Appeals,Second Circuit.\nL52: \nL53: ###\nL54: \nL55: Gershon JACOBSON, on behalf of himself and all others similarly situated, Plaintiff-Appellant, v. HEALTHCARE FINANCIAL SERVICES, INC., Defendant-Appellee.\nL56: \nL57: ### Docket No. 06-3147-cv.\nL58: \nL59: ### Decided: February 14, 2008\nL60: \nL61: ### Before: WALKER and CALABRESI, Circuit Judges, and KEENAN, District Judge.1\nL62: ### Lawrence Katz, Katz & Kleinman, Uniondale, N.Y., for Plaintiff-Appellant. Brian Miller (David J. Gold, on the brief), New York, N.Y., for Defendant-Appellee.\nL63: Plaintiff-Appellant Gershon Jacobson (“Jacobson”) appeals from a June 6, 2006 decision of Judge I. Leo Glasser, which (1) granted summary judgment to Defendant-Appellee Healthcare Financial Services (“HFS”) on Jacobson's claims under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, 15 U.S.C. § 1692 et seq.   (“FDCPA” or “the Act”), and (2) ordered Jacobson to pay attorneys' fees and costs to HFS. Jacobson v. Healthcare Fin. Servs., Inc., 434 F.Supp.2d 133 (E.D.N.Y.2006).   Jacobson appeals both determinations.\nL64: We affirm the district court in part, reverse it in part, and vacate its judgment, both as to the merits of Jacobson's claim, and as to the award of costs and attorneys' fees.   We remand the case to the district court for further proceedings consistent with this opinion.\nL65: \nL66: Background\n"
